        "execSummary":  "The persistent gap between AI technical capability and business impact is being attributed to a talent model failure: enterprises have invested in AI engineers without investing equally in the business translators who can connect AI systems to operational workflows. Anthropic\u0027s academy signals that even leading AI vendors recognize the deployment and change management challenge is as large as the model capability challenge. For enterprise AI leaders, the practical implication is that team composition — not just model selection — is a primary driver of AI ROI, and that hiring or developing business-domain AI translators is a strategic priority. Organizations relying solely on technical AI teams to drive enterprise adoption are likely underperforming their potential and should consider hybrid roles or explicit business-AI liaison functions.",
