        "summary":  "The article argues that large language models lack genuine reasoning capabilities despite appearing intelligent. Unlike AlphaGo, which combined intuition with explicit search through possible futures, current LLMs only perform fast pattern completion without maintaining an independent reasoning mechanism or inspectable epistemic state. The author advocates for developing AI systems that maintain explicit knowledge representations and follow auditable reasoning processes.",
